            <ArticleTitle>[Chronic headaches].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A207-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Under the term &quot;chronic primary headache&quot;, it is possible to distinguish several different conditions. We will describe chronic tension type headache, chronic daily headache, drug-induced headache, chronic post-traumatic headache and hemicrania continua. Each of them is a therapeutic challenge for the practitioner.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
